  "repo_truth": "Fresh immutable documentation Review 1 returned CHANGES_REQUIRED with one Critical and four Required findings: reverse Windows ReplaceFileW mutates the unexpected basis; primitive-induced ctime/USN changes make the expected-present success classifier unsatisfiable; the Windows retained-handle choreography conflicts with ReplaceFileW sharing; the new native-publication-result.json requires unapproved CRITICAL validate_transaction_inventory authority; and the machine vectors/schema do not close expected-absent, fingerprint-chain, outputless-conflict, and semantic-binding cases. All production files remain frozen and publish_replacement remains unauthorized.",
  "allowed_scope": [
    "Replay the complete 65-path subject manifest and keep every crates/** path byte-exact.",
    "Read the complete Review 1 result from the parent prompt, the atomic-publication authority documents, current control schema/vector, narrow current production feasibility surface, and primary Linux/Microsoft native API documentation.",
    "Edit only HCM-2.3 SPEC, runtime contract, control schema/vector, tasks, and the existing atomic-publication repair proof or one new documentation-remediation proof.",
    "Replace reverse Windows ReplaceFileW rollback with exact non-merging same-volume no-replace moves and specify every intermediate, error, crash, and concurrent-creation tuple.",
    "Separate stable identity/content authority from primitive-mutated post-version evidence while retaining final-boundary changed, deleted, replaced, and same-byte ABA detection.",
    "Specify executable Windows handle access/share/close choreography compatible with ReplaceFileW and correct FILE_ID_INFO authority.",
    "Add fingerprinted expected-present Unix/Windows chains, complete outputless publication_basis_conflict chain, expected-absent adapters, exact recovery rows, and semantic rejection vectors.",
    "Record the exact unapproved CRITICAL validate_transaction_inventory impact and stop; do not issue an implementation selector."
  ],
  "non_goals": [
    "No Rust, test, fixture, Cargo, dependency, preservation, archive, handoff record, ledger, staging, commit, push, HCM-2.4, Phase 3+, Phase 4, resolver redesign, public API, byte-limit, cleanup, or HCM-2.2 changes.",
    "No production implementation, no publish_replacement authority, no additional CRITICAL edit authorization, and no implementation selector.",
    "No trust in cooperating lock holders, transient authorized reader exposure, silent overwrite, metadata/stream mutation of an unexpected basis, check-only repair, wildcard recovery row, or evidence deletion."
  ],
